{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>After the art of the perfumer.</b> רֹקַח is a noun, and the accent proves it — for it is above, and it is like רֶקַח, רֶגַע; and it is not like רֹגַע הַיָּם (Isaiah 51), and like רֹקַע הָאָרֶץ (ibid. 2 Kings), where the accent is below. And anything mixed with its fellow until one exudes from the other — either scent or taste — is called מִרְקַחַת." "<b>After the art of the perfumer.</b> A compound made by craftsmanship and blendings." "<b>After the manner of the perfumer.</b> The name of the craftsman in that matter."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Rashi cites two different verses as 'שם מלכים ב' (2 Kings); the second 'ibid.' is technically a separate book, not the same as Isaiah 51."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:50.696066167Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}